    "title": "El presente simple: rutinas y la -s de he/she/it",
    "rule": "El presente simple describe rutinas: I wake up at 7:00. Con he/she/it el verbo lleva -s: She wakes up. Las horas se dicen con 'at': at 7:00, at noon, at night. Los adverbios de frecuencia (usually, always, sometimes) van antes del verbo: I usually have breakfast.",
    "examples": [
      "I wake up at 7:00.",
      "She works every day.",
      "I go to work at 8:00.",
      "We usually have lunch at 1:00.",
      "He doesn't like waking up early.",
      "Do you usually wake up early?"
    ],
    "commonMistakes": [
      "She wake up → She wakes up",
      "I usually breakfast have → I usually have breakfast",
      "a las 7 → at 7:00 (sin 'a las')"
    ]
  },
  "pronunciationTip": "La -s de la 3ª persona suena distinto: works /s/, plays /z/, watches /ɪz/. Practica: she works, she plays, she watches.",
